  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Rural Educational Institutions in Bogota as a Key Scenario for Peace Building, Promotion of Peaceful Coexistence, Reconciliation and Non-repetition</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &#x201c;Peacebuilding from the School in Bogota&#x201d; is aimed at contributing to peacebuilding, pacific coexistence, reconciliation, and non-repetition through the implementation of Bogota&#x2019;s Rural Education Policy guidelines in line with the provisions of the Peace Agreement signed between the Government of Colombia and the FARC-EP in November 2016.This project will be implemented in the 28 Rural Educational Institutions of the District (IEDR Spanish acronym) and will benefit the educational community (teachers, students, and parents), through institutional and community strengthening activities such as a) a peace course, b) the construction and dissemination of progress reports on the rural education policy, c) the construction and transfer of methodological tools to the IEDRs, and d) the implementation of pilot peace-building exercises. These activities are expected to enable the IEDRs for applying their improved capacities in the implementation of the Rural Education Policy. Likewise, these activities are expected to allow the Educational Community for applying their improved capacities to contribute to peacebuilding, reconciliation, and non-repetition</narrative>
  </description>
